# pqcrypto Project Rule

Use `AGENTS.md`, `doc/INDEX.md`, and `tool/visibility/visibility_manifest.json`
as the fast context path. The generated website, AI discovery files, Copilot
instructions, Cursor rule, and Windsurf rule all come from the visibility
manifest.

Hard constraints:
- Runtime dependencies stay at zero unless explicitly approved.
- Do not claim CMVP/FIPS 140 validation.
- Do not call the Dart implementation hard constant-time or hard zeroizing.
- Do not describe ML-KEM alone as encryption or authenticated transport.
- Preserve cookbook `you_supply` and `caveats` in generated integrations.

Evidence boundary:
- FIPS 203-aligned ML-KEM implementation with checked-in KAT evidence.
- OpenSSL interop A-G passes for ML-KEM-512/768/1024.
- FIPS 204-aligned ML-DSA implementation byte-exact on the checked-in KAT corpus.
- FIPS 205 SLH-DSA (all 12 parameter sets) byte-exact on 1,248 checked-in official NIST ACVP sample cases; unpublished development release candidate.
- Best-effort zeroization in Dart.

Before finishing visibility or documentation work:
```bash
dart run tool/visibility/generate_visibility.dart --check
git diff --check
```

Before finishing cryptographic work:
```bash
dart run tool/visibility/generate_visibility.dart --check
dart analyze
dart test test/kat_evaluator_test.dart
dart test test/mldsa_kat_test.dart
dart test test/slhdsa_kat_test.dart
dart test
dart test -p chrome
dart test -p chrome --compiler dart2wasm
dart run tool/agent_framework/check_setup.dart
```
